Opening names and ECO codes derived from:
  https://github.com/lichess-org/chess-openings  (public domain, CC0)

The file aperturas.json is generated by replaying the `pgn` column of that
dataset with chess.js and keeping the resulting EPD, so the EPD the app
computes and the EPD in the table are produced the same way and match.
Format: { "<EPD>": "<ECO>|<name>" }.

The file aperturas-lineas.json (phase 35b) is those same lines as they stand:
[eco, name, SAN moves separated by spaces], so the assistant knows that
"the Tarrasch" is 1.e4 e6 2.d4 d5 3.Nd2.
